# Add Model Server Sheet

::summary
The manual inference-endpoint sheet (RULED 08-05 — probe before confirm), opened from the Model Servers (Advanced) group's Add row: Name, Endpoint URL, Model id, Params (B), optional Bearer token. Add PROBES the endpoint before confirming — the button flips to "Probing…" and the server saves ONLY when the probe reports healthy; a failed probe keeps the sheet open with the error. No unverified server is ever saved.
::

::modal[name=add-model-server title="Add model server" width=360 placement=centered dismissible=true]

:::form[name=add-model-server submit="Add" action=addModelServer]
- Name (text, "e.g. gx10 llama.cpp") *
- Endpoint URL (text, "http://…:8723") *
- Model id (text, "Model id") *
- Params in B — optional sizing hint for routing (number)
- Bearer token — optional (password)
:::

Add → Probing… → saved only if healthy ("Model server added — healthy on :8722"). A failed probe keeps the sheet open with the error.

::

Top-right ✕ per dismiss canon. Endpoint URL and Model id render monospace and the bearer token masked (field-kind styling is renderer polish); Add stays disabled until the required fields have text.

At small width (≤ 767px, R-C ruling 08-10) the sheet goes edge-to-edge with 10px side insets and auto width; the wide placement declared on the block is unchanged.
